WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.050 --> 00:01.060
[Disclaimer: This series is created solely for entertainment purposes.

3
00:01.080 --> 00:02.330
All individuals, behaviors, places, and events depicted are entirely fictional,

4
00:02.350 --> 00:05.000
with no intention to represent or reference any organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

5
00:05.020 --> 00:06.270
Don't you think

6
00:06.400 --> 00:08.090
we ended things a bit too abruptly?

7
00:08.510 --> 00:10.940
You know why we dated back then.

8
00:10.960 --> 00:13.180
I let you use me to make other people jealous,

9
00:13.200 --> 00:14.580
but I actually love you now.

10
00:14.720 --> 00:16.090
Chris doesn't love you.

11
00:16.200 --> 00:16.860
Chris loves...

12
00:16.880 --> 00:18.130
Don't you dare say her name!

13
00:18.600 --> 00:20.000
Stop being around Chris already.

14
00:20.090 --> 00:21.280
I can't do that.

15
00:21.880 --> 00:23.000
I love Chris.

16
00:23.470 --> 00:24.900
I know everything now.

17
00:26.150 --> 00:27.600
Let's end things here.

18
00:29.320 --> 00:30.800
Chris, I'm sorry...

19
00:39.360 --> 00:41.040
Let's get back together, Chris.

20
00:42.310 --> 00:45.100
I'm the only one who has never left you.

21
00:54.600 --> 00:55.200
Chris!

22
00:55.220 --> 00:57.900
No, don't leave me. I'm sorry...

23
01:05.490 --> 01:06.520
Go to hell!

24
01:06.890 --> 01:07.720
Chris!

25
01:09.310 --> 01:10.070
Chris!

26
01:11.210 --> 01:11.730
Sun.

27
01:11.950 --> 01:13.600
I'm here. I'm right here.

28
01:17.410 --> 01:18.200
Chris...

29
01:18.630 --> 01:19.760
I'm sorry...

30
01:22.300 --> 01:23.910
It's okay now.

31
01:24.330 --> 01:25.410
It's okay. I'm right here.

32
01:26.910 --> 01:29.020
It's going to be alright.

33
01:40.760 --> 01:42.300
I'm sorry, Chris.

34
01:47.010 --> 01:48.870
What are you apologizing for?

35
02:02.320 --> 02:05.380
[Third Person]

36
02:07.600 --> 02:16.930
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

37
02:17.480 --> 02:22.610
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

38
02:22.640 --> 02:26.250
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

39
02:26.980 --> 02:32.670
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

40
02:32.690 --> 02:42.120
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

41
02:42.520 --> 02:47.570
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

42
02:47.590 --> 02:51.870
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

43
02:51.890 --> 03:00.810
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

44
03:01.250 --> 03:09.410
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

45
03:26.900 --> 03:27.590
Stress,

46
03:28.140 --> 03:29.050
anxiety,

47
03:29.070 --> 03:30.590
or uncertainty

48
03:31.150 --> 03:33.590
can make you dream about falling from a high place.

49
03:35.200 --> 03:35.960
Who was it?

50
03:37.510 --> 03:38.320
Me.

51
03:39.410 --> 03:40.800
Someone who has bizarre dreams

52
03:41.490 --> 03:44.200
and fights the voices in their head, like you,

53
03:44.600 --> 03:46.410
wouldn't ask a doctor about something so trivial.

54
03:50.390 --> 03:50.990
It's my girlfriend.

55
03:52.810 --> 03:54.710
The one you talk about a lot?

56
03:56.620 --> 03:57.600
Yeah...

57
03:58.600 --> 04:01.120
The one who makes my heart race.

58
04:02.200 --> 04:04.100
The one who made me stop fearing physical touch.

59
04:05.500 --> 04:07.000
The one I fell in love with.

60
04:08.700 --> 04:10.600
The one who made you question...

61
04:11.500 --> 04:13.400
what's real and what isn't.

62
04:16.980 --> 04:19.790
But my feelings for her are real, Doc.

63
04:21.090 --> 04:22.090
Then...

64
04:22.110 --> 04:23.220
don't be afraid of the truth.

65
04:25.210 --> 04:27.110
Can you put it more simply?

66
04:30.030 --> 04:31.370
Just tell me

67
04:31.390 --> 04:32.600
what's stressing you out

68
04:32.940 --> 04:34.300
so I can give you the right advice.

69
04:34.720 --> 04:36.260
We won't get anywhere

70
04:36.280 --> 04:37.690
if you keep beating around the bush.

71
04:38.980 --> 04:40.320
My girlfriend dreamed

72
04:40.850 --> 04:42.700
and apologized to me in her sleep.

73
04:43.850 --> 04:45.400
So I asked her why...

74
04:47.000 --> 04:48.700
I'm sorry, Chris...

75
04:50.200 --> 04:52.610
for not taking good care of myself.

76
04:53.890 --> 04:56.100
I made you worry about me.

77
04:59.580 --> 05:00.400
No,

78
05:02.600 --> 05:03.800
it's my fault.

79
05:06.160 --> 05:07.390
This is my fault.

80
05:11.300 --> 05:12.900
How is that your fault?

81
05:13.720 --> 05:15.450
I was still worried about Nadear,

82
05:15.990 --> 05:17.770
so I couldn't properly take care of Sun.

83
05:19.010 --> 05:20.010
And...

84
05:20.300 --> 05:21.550
what are you worried about with Nadear?

85
05:22.430 --> 05:23.910
It used to be about Nan.

86
05:24.720 --> 05:26.200
But now I need to think it over.

87
05:27.180 --> 05:27.950
Because

88
05:27.970 --> 05:30.710
Nan might not be Nadear's enemy as I thought.

89
05:31.590 --> 05:33.000
The easiest thing to do

90
05:33.550 --> 05:34.310
is distance yourself.

91
05:43.460 --> 05:44.880
You've come this far already.

92
05:45.000 --> 05:46.440
When are you gonna tell Chris?

93
05:46.850 --> 05:48.610
Or are you gonna let Nadear tell her herself?

94
05:49.600 --> 05:52.640
Didn't you say sleeping with her would make you more confident?

95
05:53.300 --> 05:54.590
I was wrong.

96
05:55.610 --> 05:57.000
After we slept together...

97
05:57.590 --> 05:59.320
I'm even more afraid of losing her again.

98
06:00.960 --> 06:02.090
Then choose

99
06:02.110 --> 06:04.460
whether you want to let Nadear tell her herself,

100
06:04.480 --> 06:06.520
so she can spin the story however she wants,

101
06:06.550 --> 06:08.120
or let Chris find out on her own

102
06:08.140 --> 06:09.890
and come up with all sorts of wrong ideas.

103
06:17.400 --> 06:19.760
Or are you gonna hide it from her forever?

104
06:20.400 --> 06:22.590
It wouldn't be hard to convince her since she loves you so much.

105
06:23.640 --> 06:24.590
Chris!

106
06:25.560 --> 06:27.100
You're in my room.

107
06:33.910 --> 06:34.610
Sun...

108
06:40.990 --> 06:41.800
You're right.

109
06:43.570 --> 06:45.500
If I don't tell her the truth,

110
06:46.150 --> 06:47.910
I'd be no different from Nadear.

111
06:49.600 --> 06:51.690
Chris will never be happy.

112
06:54.000 --> 06:55.880
Stop sulking, then.

113
06:56.220 --> 06:58.280
Get up, take a shower, and get to work already.

114
06:58.620 --> 06:59.570
And tonight,

115
06:59.600 --> 07:01.510
tell her the truth.

116
07:02.200 --> 07:03.610
Lie down and talk.

117
07:03.700 --> 07:06.100
Things will slowly get better that way, yeah?

118
07:07.200 --> 07:07.800
Mm.

119
07:09.010 --> 07:10.290
Thanks.

120
07:10.310 --> 07:10.910
Mm.

121
07:10.930 --> 07:11.730
I'm gonna go shower.

122
07:11.750 --> 07:12.900
Yeah, about time.

123
07:13.210 --> 07:14.210
I can smell you from here.

124
07:14.890 --> 07:15.990
Come on, get up.

125
07:21.640 --> 07:22.900
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

126
07:22.920 --> 07:26.440
You'd like to withdraw Ms. Nan's shares, correct?

127
07:26.770 --> 07:27.490
No,

128
07:27.960 --> 07:29.160
I'd like to withdraw mine.

129
07:29.590 --> 07:30.960
What are you doing?

130
07:36.670 --> 07:37.690
Answer me!

131
07:39.510 --> 07:40.500
Have you gotten better?

132
07:41.410 --> 07:42.810
You still care?

133
07:43.910 --> 07:44.610
No,

134
07:45.300 --> 07:47.920
I just want to know what you'll come up with this time.

135
07:49.940 --> 07:52.310
I already know you've been hurting yourself.

136
07:53.520 --> 07:56.800
And now I know why you let Nan keep embezzling money from our restaurant.

137
07:59.450 --> 08:01.310
If you enjoy playing the victim,

138
08:01.800 --> 08:03.900
then don't try to make me the villain, Nadear.

139
08:15.200 --> 08:17.200
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

140
08:17.220 --> 08:19.440
Are you really going to leave this restaurant?

141
08:22.100 --> 08:25.520
To be honest... I'm not that useful to this restaurant.

142
08:26.500 --> 08:27.600
That's not true.

143
08:27.790 --> 08:30.040
I've seen how hard you've worked.

144
08:30.800 --> 08:33.090
I wasn't here when this restaurant first opened,

145
08:33.110 --> 08:34.710
but didn't the restaurant's name...

146
08:35.060 --> 08:37.700
come from the three of you?

147
08:42.840 --> 08:44.960
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

148
08:49.800 --> 08:52.200
'Third Person' might not be what the name suggests anymore.

149
08:53.000 --> 08:55.900
Maybe the number three is unlucky.

150
08:57.100 --> 08:58.100
I've thought it through.

151
08:59.080 --> 09:00.510
The restaurant should belong to Nadear.

152
09:01.810 --> 09:03.190
No,

153
09:04.590 --> 09:06.310
if you're not here,

154
09:06.760 --> 09:09.400
Nan might treat Nadear even worse.

155
09:13.390 --> 09:14.510
Or maybe...

156
09:15.400 --> 09:18.370
Nan might have nothing left to use against Nadear now.

157
09:20.340 --> 09:21.300
Wawah,

158
09:22.900 --> 09:24.400
I trust you the most.

159
09:26.110 --> 09:27.520
Please take care of Nadear for me.

160
09:31.440 --> 09:32.440
[Closed]

161
10:08.610 --> 10:09.890
Why did you steal money from the restaurant?

162
10:10.400 --> 10:12.680
I thought you were here because I hurt your girlfriend.

163
10:13.500 --> 10:15.430
You and Nadear are allies, aren't you?

164
10:16.310 --> 10:17.190
No,

165
10:17.690 --> 10:19.190
I'm my own ally.

166
10:21.700 --> 10:22.390
Good.

167
10:23.290 --> 10:26.600
What do I have to do for you to tell me the truth?

168
10:27.230 --> 10:28.400
What are you planning?

169
10:33.110 --> 10:34.880
I'm selling my shares in the restaurant.

170
10:35.690 --> 10:36.810
You want them?

171
10:38.400 --> 10:41.110
You could get more than you stole.

172
10:55.890 --> 10:57.530
Why did you ring the doorbell?

173
10:57.550 --> 10:59.170
You have the keycard, don't you?

174
11:00.300 --> 11:02.210
I wanted to ask properly first.

175
11:03.710 --> 11:06.700
I might be troubling you for more than just one night this time.

176
11:11.730 --> 11:13.790
You can trouble me forever.

177
11:28.510 --> 11:29.510
Mm...

178
11:30.020 --> 11:31.090
This looks delicious.

179
11:33.110 --> 11:34.700
I bought it from the place near my clinic.

180
11:35.700 --> 11:37.110
Give it a try.

181
11:37.700 --> 11:39.690
That way, when a customer asks, you can recommend something.

182
11:42.310 --> 11:43.390
Oh, wow...

183
11:44.900 --> 11:46.190
From what I just heard,

184
11:47.010 --> 11:49.840
you're not romantic at all, Doc.

185
11:54.800 --> 11:56.730
Is it really okay to celebrate today?

186
11:59.090 --> 12:01.580
You just went through something uncomfortable, didn't you?

187
12:11.980 --> 12:14.990
It's something I should've done a while ago.

188
12:16.510 --> 12:18.100
If we're going to live together,

189
12:18.400 --> 12:19.600
we should talk things through like this.

190
12:21.120 --> 12:22.310
It's pretty realistic.

191
12:25.300 --> 12:27.000
I'm a pro at buying cheap food.

192
12:28.400 --> 12:30.280
Work keeps me busy enough already.

193
12:32.260 --> 12:33.080
Mm.

194
12:34.010 --> 12:36.120
That sounds nice.

195
12:38.110 --> 12:39.110
How?

196
12:41.910 --> 12:44.000
How we're going to live together from now on.

197
12:53.800 --> 12:54.920
Chris...

198
12:55.800 --> 12:58.100
I have to work at the clinic

199
12:59.100 --> 13:01.190
to pay back the debt I owe my father.

200
13:04.320 --> 13:06.310
I don't have anything I can call my own.

201
13:08.110 --> 13:09.310
Whether it's a house

202
13:10.700 --> 13:11.510
or a car.

203
13:15.210 --> 13:17.400
My father spent so much money

204
13:19.200 --> 13:21.400
sending me abroad for treatment.

205
13:24.190 --> 13:27.510
You were sent abroad for treatment?

206
13:29.700 --> 13:30.700
Chris...

207
13:32.000 --> 13:33.380
The truth is...

208
13:49.220 --> 13:50.280
Sun...

209
13:50.590 --> 13:51.200
Sun.

210
13:52.300 --> 13:53.510
Sun? What's wrong?

211
13:55.100 --> 13:55.810
Sun?

212
13:56.550 --> 13:57.910
Are you alright?

213
13:59.400 --> 14:00.980
Sun, are you okay?

214
14:03.100 --> 14:06.300
[Third Person]

215
14:08.411 --> 14:11.391
[Third Person]

216
14:27.091 --> 14:28.781
Are you sure you're alright?

217
14:30.181 --> 14:31.601
Shouldn't you go see a doctor?

218
14:33.351 --> 14:34.691
Chris, I'm a doctor.

219
14:36.311 --> 14:37.881
I know I'll be fine.

220
14:41.141 --> 14:42.801
But I'm your girlfriend,

221
14:43.371 --> 14:44.591
and I don't know that.

222
14:45.071 --> 14:46.271
I'm worried about you.

223
14:55.781 --> 14:57.031
I'll be alright.

224
14:57.601 --> 14:58.601
Really?

225
15:00.171 --> 15:00.781
Mm.

226
15:01.901 --> 15:03.091
It's just a migraine.

227
15:04.081 --> 15:05.571
The clinic just opened.

228
15:06.021 --> 15:07.101
There's so much to do.

229
15:09.201 --> 15:10.201
Then...

230
15:10.961 --> 15:12.311
can you try not to stress so much?

231
15:13.381 --> 15:15.221
Or at least share it with me

232
15:15.241 --> 15:16.541
when you are stressed?

233
15:18.491 --> 15:20.671
You can tell me anything.

234
15:24.791 --> 15:25.751
Yes, babe.

235
15:27.081 --> 15:29.191
First things first, take a shower.

236
15:32.041 --> 15:32.901
What about you, Sun?

237
15:34.281 --> 15:35.701
Go on ahead.

238
15:41.601 --> 15:42.581
Alright,

239
15:46.091 --> 15:48.601
I'll help you relax.

240
15:53.451 --> 15:54.481
Chris?

241
15:58.251 --> 15:59.531
What are you doing?

242
16:00.381 --> 16:01.381
Chris!

243
16:16.501 --> 16:19.391
That headache came back.

244
16:19.791 --> 16:22.031
[That headache came back]

245
16:28.151 --> 16:29.331
Your medical history shows

246
16:29.351 --> 16:33.091
that you had a tumor near the brainstem.

247
16:33.791 --> 16:36.421
Tumors near the brainstem

248
16:36.441 --> 16:38.791
are at high risk of recurring.

249
16:38.991 --> 16:40.581
It's a good thing you came in early.

250
16:43.291 --> 16:45.491
Will it come back?

251
16:46.421 --> 16:48.581
I can't say for sure yet.

252
16:48.611 --> 16:50.911
I need to examine you thoroughly first.

253
17:08.431 --> 17:10.751
Chris, you're back?

254
17:18.691 --> 17:19.691
Dr. Jeen.

255
17:20.851 --> 17:21.891
Jeen.

256
17:22.991 --> 17:24.211
Call me Jeen.

257
17:25.391 --> 17:26.801
It doesn't matter what I call you.

258
17:34.691 --> 17:35.481
It does.

259
17:37.401 --> 17:38.791
I'm not just a doctor.

260
17:41.111 --> 17:42.601
I'm yours, Nadear.

261
17:47.991 --> 17:48.991
Why are you here?

262
17:53.311 --> 17:54.581
Chris already left.

263
17:56.451 --> 17:57.791
I came to see you.

264
17:58.791 --> 18:00.291
Chris already left,

265
18:00.911 --> 18:02.251
but you're still here.

266
18:03.781 --> 18:05.271
You have to keep going.

267
18:08.871 --> 18:11.301
Are you here to see if I'm dead yet?

268
18:15.201 --> 18:16.511
If I am,

269
18:17.091 --> 18:19.211
just know it was your fault.

270
18:19.711 --> 18:22.511
Because you're stupid and can't do anything right.

271
18:23.311 --> 18:25.501
You made her leave me!

272
18:26.541 --> 18:28.681
I have no one left.

273
18:46.671 --> 18:48.471
You can say whatever you want to me,

274
18:51.611 --> 18:52.691
but don't say

275
18:54.691 --> 18:56.111
that you have no one left.

276
19:18.881 --> 19:20.501
It might take some time,

277
19:21.381 --> 19:22.591
but things will get better.

278
19:24.741 --> 19:25.971
Thank you, Doc.

279
19:28.201 --> 19:30.911
I can rest easy with you by her side.

280
19:33.171 --> 19:33.911
Yeah.

281
19:35.361 --> 19:36.571
I...

282
19:36.591 --> 19:38.091
should have realized sooner.

283
19:39.721 --> 19:40.781
What do you mean?

284
19:41.641 --> 19:42.371
It's nothing.

285
19:43.601 --> 19:44.711
Like I said before,

286
19:45.441 --> 19:47.231
you can't help how you feel.

287
19:48.391 --> 19:50.431
If you're going to leave Nadear,

288
19:51.071 --> 19:52.491
don't ever go back to her.

289
19:53.611 --> 19:56.031
Don't give her hope again.

290
19:57.601 --> 19:58.761
And...

291
19:59.071 --> 20:00.381
you don't have to worry about her.

292
20:02.721 --> 20:04.231
I can take care of her.

293
20:05.491 --> 20:06.751
The truth is...

294
20:08.191 --> 20:09.691
I've always taken care of Nadear.

295
20:11.651 --> 20:13.911
You're the best friend I've ever had.

296
20:24.201 --> 20:25.011
I'll get going now.

297
20:25.311 --> 20:25.891
Mm.

298
20:33.991 --> 20:35.201
I'm sorry, Chris.

299
20:37.291 --> 20:39.381
I couldn't even bring myself to tell you

300
20:41.411 --> 20:42.871
that this is my fault.

301
21:01.171 --> 21:02.071
Nadear!

302
21:23.511 --> 21:28.071
[Craniopharyngioma]

303
21:54.571 --> 21:56.491
Babe.

304
21:56.861 --> 21:57.601
Hey,

305
21:58.591 --> 21:59.891
I brought this for you.

306
22:05.901 --> 22:07.481
Dust can trigger migraines, right?

307
22:07.501 --> 22:09.371
That's why I brought you this air-purifying plant.

308
22:09.391 --> 22:11.081
You can keep it indoors,

309
22:11.101 --> 22:13.311
and it helps purify the air.

310
22:16.201 --> 22:17.791
You're the best.

311
22:18.591 --> 22:19.631
Right?

312
22:19.971 --> 22:22.631
You won't find a girlfriend like me anywhere else.

313
22:40.511 --> 22:41.371
Yeah.

314
22:42.301 --> 22:43.991
Nowhere else.

315
22:53.301 --> 22:54.391
What's wrong?

316
22:55.861 --> 22:57.401
Are you stressed about the clinic?

317
23:03.271 --> 23:05.611
I'm planning to sell Nadear my shares in the restaurant.

318
23:05.631 --> 23:06.991
I should get a decent amount for them.

319
23:07.701 --> 23:09.831
If you need more money, just tell me.

320
23:11.411 --> 23:13.631
But don't stress yourself out or get sick again, okay?

321
23:21.491 --> 23:23.101
I'm fine.

322
23:24.591 --> 23:25.691
I'm not sick.

323
23:26.791 --> 23:28.281
I'm staying here with you.

324
23:32.551 --> 23:34.071
Aw...

325
23:34.471 --> 23:36.101
You're so stressed out, aren't you?

326
23:37.801 --> 23:39.511
It's okay.

327
23:41.401 --> 23:42.231
How about this?

328
23:44.211 --> 23:45.601
Let's go to the flower farm tomorrow.

329
23:48.191 --> 23:48.871
Yeah.

330
24:28.821 --> 24:30.831
Aw...

331
24:33.221 --> 24:34.491
Don't be sad.

332
24:35.001 --> 24:36.111
I'm the one who's sick,

333
24:36.381 --> 24:38.031
not you.

334
24:38.571 --> 24:39.501
But...

335
24:39.521 --> 24:40.781
how can you be so calm?

336
24:42.111 --> 24:43.391
I'm not.

337
24:44.601 --> 24:46.871
But the doctor did say it could come back.

338
24:48.961 --> 24:51.351
Can you act a little sadder?

339
24:52.001 --> 24:52.891
Nope.

340
24:54.641 --> 24:56.291
If it comes back, I have to get treatment.

341
24:56.641 --> 24:57.951
I have to get better.

342
25:00.181 --> 25:02.191
I won't lose Chris again.

343
25:02.801 --> 25:04.301
What if you forget everything again?

344
25:05.481 --> 25:06.891
I've forgotten before.

345
25:07.511 --> 25:09.111
Chris has, too.

346
25:10.081 --> 25:12.491
Some memories might fade.

347
25:13.991 --> 25:15.831
But if the feelings are still there,

348
25:17.391 --> 25:18.631
I believe...

349
25:19.471 --> 25:20.791
as long as we still love each other,

350
25:21.291 --> 25:22.691
we'll always love each other.

351
25:28.221 --> 25:30.291
And now I have you here.

352
25:31.781 --> 25:33.081
If I forget again,

353
25:34.201 --> 25:36.701
you'll take me to Chris, right?

354
25:36.721 --> 25:38.561
- Mm... - Right?

355
25:38.591 --> 25:40.131
Sure,

356
25:40.151 --> 25:41.091
smarty.

357
25:41.591 --> 25:42.671
But first things first,

358
25:43.051 --> 25:45.311
you have to tell Chris the truth

359
25:45.611 --> 25:47.631
before you forget again.

360
25:48.911 --> 25:50.591
Yes, Mom.

361
25:51.391 --> 25:52.871
You've got this, my girl.

362
25:56.691 --> 25:57.691
Chris,

363
25:58.671 --> 26:00.781
I won't make the same mistake again.

364
26:09.101 --> 26:10.101
Yes, Jeen?

365
26:27.701 --> 26:28.381
Sun!

366
26:31.921 --> 26:32.631
Sun.

367
26:32.651 --> 26:33.581
Sun.

368
26:34.361 --> 26:35.001
Sun.

369
26:39.301 --> 26:43.201
[Third Person]

370
26:44.521 --> 26:48.291
[Third Person]

371
26:50.051 --> 26:51.851
You were stressed and hadn't eaten,

372
26:51.871 --> 26:52.871
and your blood pressure dropped.

373
26:53.481 --> 26:54.761
Why didn't you tell me?

374
26:56.861 --> 26:57.861
I was excited

375
27:00.311 --> 27:01.731
about going to the flower farm.

376
27:02.431 --> 27:03.761
And we had to cut the trip short.

377
27:03.781 --> 27:04.821
Isn't that great, huh?

378
27:05.401 --> 27:06.791
Can you take me there again?

379
27:10.431 --> 27:11.691
Eat first.

380
27:17.211 --> 27:18.331
I'll take you there tomorrow.

381
27:27.001 --> 27:28.301
You stubborn girl.

382
27:30.801 --> 27:32.091
Will you still love me, then?

383
27:33.891 --> 27:36.701
I won't if you don't take care of yourself.

384
27:44.181 --> 27:45.571
One more bite.

385
27:55.081 --> 27:55.791
Sun,

386
27:56.851 --> 27:58.111
I have something to tell you.

387
27:59.401 --> 28:01.421
But don't worry too much, okay?

388
28:03.471 --> 28:05.081
How can I not worry

389
28:05.541 --> 28:06.991
when you start by saying that?

390
28:08.591 --> 28:09.671
Nadear tried to kill herself...

391
28:10.491 --> 28:11.171
Huh...?

392
28:11.591 --> 28:13.381
But I'm not going back to her.

393
28:15.311 --> 28:18.901
I know Nadear might use this to make me stay with her.

394
28:22.741 --> 28:25.291
I'm just going to see the doctor who treated me.

395
28:26.291 --> 28:28.181
She's taking care of Nadear now.

396
28:30.851 --> 28:32.371
What about you? Are you alright?

397
28:41.891 --> 28:43.601
I think it's partly my fault.

398
28:45.281 --> 28:47.991
I always gave Nadear what she wanted,

399
28:48.831 --> 28:51.041
and I think that pushed her to this point.

400
28:53.681 --> 28:55.871
I want to help you, too.

401
29:08.681 --> 29:10.591
As long as you're healthy, that's enough for me.

402
29:11.891 --> 29:14.881
Just having you in this world already helps me so much.

403
29:18.171 --> 29:19.801
I'll live for you, Chris.

404
30:12.821 --> 30:13.591
Nadear!

405
30:14.511 --> 30:15.291
Nadear?!

406
30:16.711 --> 30:17.461
Nadear!

407
30:17.991 --> 30:19.491
Leave me alone!

408
30:19.801 --> 30:21.711
You betrayed me!

409
30:21.741 --> 30:23.701
Nadear, I'm sorry!

410
30:24.631 --> 30:25.791
I'll do it...

411
30:28.151 --> 30:30.291
I'll make Chris yours again.

412
30:31.111 --> 30:32.401
I'm sorry...

413
30:32.981 --> 30:34.291
I'll do it for you, Nadear.

414
30:36.421 --> 30:37.121
Nadear...

415
30:37.511 --> 30:39.691
Nadear, Nadear... Nadear!

416
30:39.941 --> 30:40.881
Nadear!

417
31:05.651 --> 31:07.191
What happened to Nadear, Doc?

418
31:08.591 --> 31:10.401
Nadear is really upset over losing you.

419
31:11.201 --> 31:12.901
So I told her

420
31:12.921 --> 31:14.371
I'd help you regain your memories

421
31:15.011 --> 31:16.111
so this could finally end.

422
31:17.221 --> 31:18.381
But she wouldn't accept that,

423
31:19.401 --> 31:20.401
so she acted out of spite.

424
31:23.561 --> 31:25.191
Help me remember?

425
31:26.791 --> 31:27.791
What do you mean?

426
31:32.201 --> 31:32.891
Chris,

427
31:33.701 --> 31:34.701
I'm sorry.

428
31:36.531 --> 31:38.291
The hypnosis I performed on you

429
31:38.721 --> 31:40.491
wasn't meant to help you remember,

430
31:41.261 --> 31:42.601
but to make you forget.

431
31:50.731 --> 31:51.791
Why...?

432
31:56.301 --> 31:58.391
Because if you knew the truth,

433
32:00.311 --> 32:02.291
you might not be able to stay with Nadear.

434
32:03.661 --> 32:04.501
And...

435
32:05.711 --> 32:07.811
Nadear can't lose you, either.

436
32:08.501 --> 32:09.801
What truth?

437
32:13.301 --> 32:14.911
The truth between you and Sun.

438
32:26.481 --> 32:28.201
I'll have to...

439
32:28.231 --> 32:29.591
tell you the truth,

440
32:30.791 --> 32:32.601
because I don't know what to do anymore.

441
32:35.081 --> 32:36.791
Do you still want to know the truth?

442
32:38.711 --> 32:40.111
The truth.

443
32:42.861 --> 32:45.881
You mean my real memories?

444
33:15.401 --> 33:16.711
She still hasn't answered?

445
33:20.691 --> 33:24.601
Are you going to have surgery here, or go back to your previous doctor?

446
33:30.791 --> 33:31.791
I'll have surgery here.

447
33:34.091 --> 33:35.491
I have to get better,

448
33:37.191 --> 33:38.881
and remember everything, too.

449
34:12.911 --> 34:13.801
Sun,

450
34:16.391 --> 34:18.901
that girl with dark hair.

451
34:20.151 --> 34:21.691
She's quiet and reserved.

452
34:23.401 --> 34:25.901
She was your only close friend

453
34:26.241 --> 34:27.571
in middle school.

454
34:44.901 --> 34:45.691
Sun

455
34:47.021 --> 34:48.091
was your

456
34:48.111 --> 34:50.171
most important friend.

457
34:51.711 --> 34:53.001
Until...

458
34:53.671 --> 34:54.671
Nadear

459
34:55.261 --> 34:56.811
came along and became your new friend.

460
35:00.101 --> 35:00.691
Here.

461
35:08.191 --> 35:09.191
Hey, wait!

462
35:09.901 --> 35:10.611
Chris!

463
35:48.681 --> 35:50.601
Who...is Sun?

464
35:55.101 --> 35:56.011
My best friend.

465
35:56.541 --> 35:57.491
That's right.

466
35:59.191 --> 36:00.251
Sun...

467
36:01.521 --> 36:02.691
is your best friend

468
36:03.531 --> 36:05.591
who's been secretly in love with you all along.

469
36:43.691 --> 36:45.671
I love the smell of your shampoo.

470
36:48.771 --> 36:50.981
Hey, it's okay now,

471
36:51.001 --> 36:52.401
my dear.

472
37:28.081 --> 37:29.851
Is Nadear alright?

473
37:42.691 --> 37:44.881
The doctors are keeping a close eye on her.

474
37:50.041 --> 37:51.101
What about you?

475
37:52.691 --> 37:53.691
Are you alright?

476
37:56.061 --> 37:57.801
Are you feeling any better?

477
37:59.791 --> 38:01.801
Seeing a friend in that state

478
38:02.421 --> 38:04.391
must have been really upsetting.

479
38:14.991 --> 38:17.001
Why do you know me so well?

480
38:19.181 --> 38:20.311
Of course I do.

481
38:21.531 --> 38:22.791
The Chris I love

482
38:23.311 --> 38:26.091
always puts others before herself.

483
38:30.201 --> 38:31.881
What about the Sun I love?

484
38:34.201 --> 38:35.591
I'm yours.

485
38:51.801 --> 38:52.981
You smell nicer than the roses.

486
38:57.781 --> 38:59.111
You smell even better.

487
39:02.291 --> 39:03.801
Have you gotten better?

488
39:03.891 --> 39:05.121
Getting all feisty like this.

489
39:06.301 --> 39:07.691
I feel better now.

490
39:10.431 --> 39:11.431
Then...

491
39:11.451 --> 39:12.281
Let's go.

492
39:13.611 --> 39:14.511
Where to?

493
39:15.911 --> 39:17.591
To pay for the damages.

494
39:18.201 --> 39:20.061
You fell on a bunch of flowers

495
39:20.091 --> 39:22.261
and crushed so many of them last time.

496
39:23.021 --> 39:24.001
Chris!

497
39:24.531 --> 39:25.911
Just kidding.

498
39:26.591 --> 39:29.101
You said you wanted to go to the flower farm, after all.

499
39:29.691 --> 39:30.981
Let's go, then.

500
39:33.161 --> 39:33.901
Yes,

501
39:37.921 --> 39:39.901
I want to go everywhere with you.

502
39:41.301 --> 39:43.571
Whether it's somewhere we've been, somewhere new,

503
39:44.301 --> 39:45.991
or the same place over and over.

504
39:47.001 --> 39:49.011
As long as you're there with me.

505
39:51.801 --> 39:52.911
Of course,

506
39:52.941 --> 39:54.691
I'll go everywhere with you.

507
40:23.791 --> 40:27.891
[Third Person]

508
40:29.468 --> 40:32.958
[Third Person]

509
40:46.548 --> 40:47.838
Jeen...

510
40:49.948 --> 40:51.568
It's alright now, Nadear.

511
40:58.448 --> 40:59.848
Promise...

512
41:02.178 --> 41:03.458
Don't worry.

513
41:04.178 --> 41:05.948
I did what you asked.

514
41:21.278 --> 41:22.268
Did you know?

515
41:22.288 --> 41:24.268
Going everywhere with you

516
41:24.288 --> 41:25.958
has always been my dream.

517
41:28.028 --> 41:29.148
You love going out, huh?

518
41:30.268 --> 41:31.958
I just like traveling.

519
41:33.948 --> 41:34.828
Why?

520
41:36.548 --> 41:39.158
Maybe because it feels endless.

521
41:40.448 --> 41:41.648
Especially

522
41:41.668 --> 41:43.538
now that we're really together.

523
41:44.758 --> 41:48.968
It feels like this moment is truly ours.

524
41:51.648 --> 41:54.328
But if you faint again, I won't take you there anymore.

525
41:57.878 --> 41:59.268
If I faint again,

526
41:59.998 --> 42:01.528
I probably won't get to go anymore.

527
42:03.408 --> 42:04.568
That's odd.

528
42:04.588 --> 42:05.838
Is something wrong?

529
42:07.198 --> 42:08.368
It's nothing.

530
42:08.748 --> 42:09.748
I mean...

531
42:10.368 --> 42:12.538
you won't take me there anymore, right?

532
42:27.918 --> 42:28.918
There you are.

533
42:30.648 --> 42:31.558
What's on your mind?

534
42:33.138 --> 42:35.358
Last time, I fainted among the flowers.

535
42:36.188 --> 42:37.958
Not exactly the best of memory.

536
42:39.168 --> 42:42.018
I don't want you to remember me that way.

537
42:42.948 --> 42:45.558
But every moment we spent together,

538
42:46.918 --> 42:48.948
either good or bad,

539
42:50.348 --> 42:52.258
I'll always cherish them.

540
42:53.388 --> 42:54.728
I have something for you.

541
42:58.698 --> 42:59.428
Rose.

542
43:00.508 --> 43:01.938
The flower that brought us together.

543
43:09.258 --> 43:09.978
Here.

544
43:20.958 --> 43:22.438
Thank you so much, Sun.

545
43:25.478 --> 43:27.388
I have something to tell you.

546
43:28.748 --> 43:29.938
I...

547
43:29.958 --> 43:31.038
I already knew that.

548
43:41.558 --> 43:42.558
Where is Chris?

549
43:43.568 --> 43:45.278
I told her to go.

550
43:45.938 --> 43:47.028
Where to?

551
43:47.748 --> 43:48.848
To settle things

552
43:49.348 --> 43:50.528
one last time.

553
43:52.248 --> 43:53.948
Are you tricking me again?

554
43:54.798 --> 43:55.848
You know full well

555
43:56.478 --> 43:58.748
what I'm most afraid of.

556
44:01.858 --> 44:03.668
I love you, Jeen.

557
44:21.378 --> 44:22.258
You...?

558
44:23.268 --> 44:24.028
Nan?

559
44:25.968 --> 44:26.988
That's right!

560
44:27.368 --> 44:28.858
Didn't you say you'd drop it?!

561
44:30.268 --> 44:32.338
Then what's this police summons doing at my house?!

562
44:32.358 --> 44:33.578
Stop... Stop!

563
44:35.078 --> 44:37.548
You want me to tell Chris the truth, right?

564
44:37.838 --> 44:39.828
Stop threatening me with Chris.

565
44:41.568 --> 44:42.248
Why?

566
44:42.758 --> 44:44.468
Got yourself a new partner?

567
44:44.768 --> 44:46.448
If the summons is taking too long,

568
44:46.848 --> 44:50.178
why not spend a night in jail for trespassing instead?

569
44:50.278 --> 44:51.098
Nadear!

570
44:54.048 --> 44:55.268
The money you embezzled

571
44:55.288 --> 44:57.508
should be more than enough for you to live in luxury.

572
44:57.758 --> 44:59.128
I reported you to the police

573
44:59.148 --> 45:02.108
because you're greedy, stupid, and useless.

574
45:02.648 --> 45:04.548
If you'd kept quiet and done nothing,

575
45:05.438 --> 45:07.548
would Chris have left me?!

576
45:08.238 --> 45:09.748
Stop acting all innocent.

577
45:13.868 --> 45:16.448
See what I've had to go through

578
45:16.468 --> 45:17.818
because you didn't do enough to help me?

579
45:30.958 --> 45:32.348
What are you to that crazy bitch?

580
45:34.098 --> 45:37.138
I won't let anyone harm Nadear.

581
45:37.448 --> 45:39.338
I'll prove it by...

582
45:39.758 --> 45:41.758
If you don't leave this house right away,

583
45:42.358 --> 45:43.438
I'm calling the police.

584
46:01.708 --> 46:03.138
Chris, I'm sorry.

585
46:03.748 --> 46:05.938
It's too late for me to turn back now.

586
46:08.458 --> 46:09.558
What did you know?

587
46:12.258 --> 46:14.138
I remember who you were.

588
46:21.288 --> 46:21.838
Here.

589
46:22.058 --> 46:23.538
She gave it to me

590
46:23.558 --> 46:25.658
before Buddhism class.

591
46:35.698 --> 46:36.628
Hey, wait!

592
46:37.348 --> 46:38.108
Chris!

593
46:45.138 --> 46:46.838
Have you finished copying my homework?

594
46:47.488 --> 46:49.278
Not yet. Are you going to turn it in now?

595
46:49.838 --> 46:50.598
It's alright.

596
46:50.618 --> 46:51.648
I'll wait until you're done.

597
46:52.678 --> 46:53.628
Give me a sec.

598
46:58.858 --> 46:59.858
Chris...

599
47:03.778 --> 47:04.928
It's alright now.

600
47:12.858 --> 47:14.348
My parents...

601
47:16.848 --> 47:19.038
they're gone.

602
47:29.658 --> 47:33.348
I feel like Sun got my dog killed on purpose.

603
47:34.748 --> 47:37.448
Sun isn't heartless, Nadear.

604
47:38.368 --> 47:39.558
You know that.

605
47:39.578 --> 47:40.928
She's my friend.

606
47:41.558 --> 47:43.698
A friend who secretly loves you?

607
47:47.268 --> 47:48.268
Nadear...

608
47:53.368 --> 47:54.838
Did you and Nadear fight again?

609
47:55.648 --> 47:56.338
Mm.

610
47:57.468 --> 47:59.238
Nadear never understands me.

611
48:00.548 --> 48:02.068
What is it this time?

612
48:05.278 --> 48:06.348
It's about you.

613
48:08.248 --> 48:09.558
A girlfriend and a best friend.

614
48:10.038 --> 48:11.038
It's nothing new.

615
48:17.398 --> 48:18.828
Nadear told me you love me.

616
48:19.468 --> 48:20.738
How could that be?

617
48:21.388 --> 48:23.248
We've known each other since middle school.

618
48:35.948 --> 48:36.948
Right...

619
48:37.648 --> 48:39.638
We've known each other since middle school.

620
48:40.648 --> 48:42.548
So if you're going to love someone,

621
48:43.438 --> 48:44.638
why can't it be me?

622
49:04.458 --> 49:05.458
Chris,

623
49:05.848 --> 49:07.228
I'm sorry...

624
49:07.758 --> 49:10.138
I thought I already closed the door.

625
49:10.658 --> 49:12.508
I didn't think that Nadear would see us.

626
49:13.148 --> 49:14.048
Forget it.

627
49:14.238 --> 49:16.468
Right now, we have to find Nadear.

628
49:16.638 --> 49:17.948
She was furious.

629
49:18.558 --> 49:20.108
I can't lose her.

630
49:22.518 --> 49:23.838
If you still love her,

631
49:25.148 --> 49:26.658
then why are you with me?

632
49:29.068 --> 49:30.348
I'm sorry, Sun.

633
49:30.898 --> 49:31.948
But I love Nadear.

634
49:40.168 --> 49:42.128
Nadear doesn't want me to remember,

635
49:43.168 --> 49:44.668
so I won't have to feel guilty.

636
49:45.748 --> 49:48.858
But she probably didn't think I'd make the same mistake twice.

637
49:49.758 --> 49:50.838
No...

638
49:52.348 --> 49:53.538
I know

639
49:54.338 --> 49:56.248
why you apologized to me now.

640
49:58.048 --> 49:59.558
That's not it, Chris.

641
50:00.258 --> 50:02.028
We both betrayed Nadear.

642
50:03.178 --> 50:05.828
We made her this way.

643
50:08.168 --> 50:09.668
I do love you,

644
50:12.988 --> 50:15.468
but our relationship was wrong from the beginning.

645
50:23.138 --> 50:26.988
♫Trapped in a love that's a fading image,♫

646
50:27.008 --> 50:30.728
♫Yet the love that never faded♫

647
50:30.748 --> 50:33.778
♫Like a missing page♫

648
50:33.798 --> 50:37.198
♫I can't find♫

649
50:37.218 --> 50:40.308
♫Your smell lingers vividly in my mind♫

650
50:43.368 --> 50:44.958
Stop talking,

651
50:45.168 --> 50:46.228
and listen to me.

652
50:47.048 --> 50:50.518
♫You're still so clear in my heart♫

653
50:50.538 --> 50:54.418
♫But who are you?♫

654
50:54.438 --> 50:57.498
♫...Please tell me♫

655
50:57.568 --> 50:59.788
I won't let Chris stay with Nadear anymore.

656
50:59.838 --> 51:01.308
I have to save her.

657
51:01.758 --> 51:02.908
I promise

658
51:03.058 --> 51:04.548
I won't make the same mistake again.

659
51:04.568 --> 51:05.678
From now on,

660
51:05.698 --> 51:07.658
there will be just the two of us.

661
51:07.678 --> 51:09.628
I'm living

662
51:09.668 --> 51:11.328
for you right now, Jeen.

663
51:11.348 --> 51:13.358
I want to end this, too.

664
51:13.708 --> 51:15.738
